"""STT push-to-talk daemon: hold the trigger key (Menu unless Settings says
otherwise; F24 when kanata's Squelch tap-hold sits on it) to record
from the mic picked in Settings (default: PipeWire's default source),
beamform + clean, transcribe with the resident Parakeet or Whisper server
(Vulkan GPU), and paste the result via clipboard + Shift+Insert (Ctrl+V
in browsers), or type it through the active keyboard layout. Optionally
words are typed while you speak, each one once the model is sure of it.
The tray shows a pill while it listens and transcribes.

Usage:
  squelch-ptt                run the daemon (systemd user service does this)
  squelch-ptt --process F    DSP + transcribe file F, print result (no typing,
                             no stats or archive; F is left alone)
  squelch-ptt --probe-mic    record 2.5 s, report whether the mic delivers audio
  squelch-ptt --reset-mic    power-cycle the mic's USB port and re-probe
"""
